The effect of contact time on the adsorption capacities of GAC and the synthesized nanocomposites was investigated by using a known concentration of Pb2+ ion solution (1000 ppm, 100.0 cm3) in the time span of 15–180 min. The temperature was kept constant at room temperature with random stirring. The adsorbent was subjected to filtration from the solution and the filtrate was analyzed using atomic absorption spectroscopy for the residual Pb2+ ion concentration. The adsorption capacity was evaluated using the general equation given below.1\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
