				\begin{document}$$\log Q_{e} \; = \;\log K_{f} \; + \;\frac{1}{n}\log C_{e}$$\end{document}logQe=logKf+1nlogCe

The Langmuir isotherm linearized form written as given in Eq. (3) where the constants qm and K, are related to the adsorption capacity and the energy of adsorption, respectively. The graph of Ce/Qe vs Ce was plotted to determine the Langmuir isotherm constants [42, 43].3\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
